request: Make the output easier to read. --behaviour

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different output changes (showing ids, showing due dates, lining up columns, sorting, colour, a summary line). Each one changes the existing format tests differently, so I need to know which ones you want before I can write a testable spec.)
governor asks: Which changes do you want? Right now `todo list` prints lines like `[ ] buy milk` and `[x] walk dog`. It doesn't show ids (which you need for `todo complete`) or due dates. Here's my suggestion:
1. Show the id on each line, e.g. `#1 [ ] buy milk`.
2. Show the due date when there is one, e.g. `#1 [ ] buy milk  (due 2026-11-01)`.
3. Line up the titles in columns so the due dates line up too.
4. Optional: sort open todos first, then by due date (earliest first), with done todos at the end.
5. Optional: add a summary line at the end, e.g. `2 open, 1 done`.
6. Optional: colour (for example, done items greyed out). This only works in terminals that support colour.
Should I do 1–3? Tell me which of 4–6 you also want, or describe a different format you have in mind.

